  "title": "Kirby Problem 2.26",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(Kontsevich–Zorich conjecture). Understand the homotopy types\nof strata of abelian differentials. Which stratum-components are $K(\\pi, 1)$ spaces?\nWhat are the fundamental groups? For which stratum-components $\\mathcal{H}$ is some ver-\nsion of the monodromy map $\\rho: \\pi_{1}(\\mathcal{H}) \\to \\operatorname{Mod}(S_{g})$ injective? Do the answers to\nthese questions change in a predictable way as one moves from the principal stra-\ntum down to the minimal?",
